  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Circular Economy Resource Centre</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;div&gt;The &lt;b&gt;EU Circular Economy Resource Centre (EU CERC) &lt;/b&gt;is a 5-year project funded by the European Union and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Finland and implemented by the Finnish Innovation Fund Sitra and the Belgian Agency for International Cooperation - Enabel. It aims to increase the uptake of &lt;b&gt;sound and inclusive Circular Economy policies and business models, based on peer-to-peer exchanges and partnerships between EU and third country stakeholders&lt;/b&gt; through three complementary labs: the Policy lab, the Knowledge lab and the Business Lab.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- The &lt;b&gt;Policy Lab &lt;/b&gt;supports the development and implementation of circular economy policies and road maps in partner countries.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- The &lt;b&gt;Knowledge Lab&lt;/b&gt; offers partnership and collaboration support between EU and partner countries and matches demand for support with supply by facilitating the exchange of circular economy knowledge and best practices.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- The &lt;b&gt;Business Lab&lt;/b&gt;, implemented by Enabel, Supports the circular economy transition for enterprises and business support organizations in partner countries and strengthens collaboration between EU and partner countries&#x2019; enterprises.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The EU CERC offers&amp;nbsp; collaboration support, peer-to-peer learning, technical assistance, expertise and compliance support. The EU CERC operates on a broad scale; activities will take place across Africa, the Eastern and Southern Neighbourhood, Asia, Latin America and the Caribbean.&lt;/div&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
